---
const posts = [
  {
    title: "On-chain KPIs every founder should forge first",
    desc: "The seven metrics every protocol should watch from day one: wallet retention, real depth, concentration risk and more.",
  },
  {
    title: "Spellbook: dbt models that survive the next hard fork",
    desc: "Patterns and anti-patterns when you contribute to Dune's public spellbook for a fast-moving chain.",
  },
  {
    title: "Giedi Lab: multi-chain user attribution",
    desc: "Our ongoing work on understanding a user that moves across five chains and two bridges, without doxxing them.",
  },
];
---

<section id="blog">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div class="label">Blog</div>
    <div class="pager">P[1]/3</div>
  </div>

  <div class="blog-lead">
    <div class="blog-thumb"><span>Giedi</span></div>
    <div>
      <h4 class="blog-title">Designing a Dune dashboard that actually gets used</h4>
      <p class="blog-excerpt">
        A dashboard is a product. What we measure, how we name it and the story each row tells.
        Lessons from 40+ deliveries for protocols on Ethereum, Solana and L2s.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {
    posts.map((p) => (
      <div class="blog-row">
        <div class="rt">{p.title}</div>
        <div class="rd">{p.desc}</div>
      </div>
    ))
  }
</section>
